---
name: ui-assess
description: "Assess an existing UI, workflow or implementation for concrete defects and prioritized improvements. Use for review-only work or the assessment stage of a Studio run."
---

# Assess the current state

Implementation target: activate with compatible Studio commands.

## Inputs and scope

Read the goal, current artifact/build, target users/tasks, repository instructions, supported surfaces and requested review scope. Inspection is read-only unless edits are separately authorized. Resolve exact versions and distinguish supplied claims from observations.

## Workflow

Inspect real artifacts and representative complete workflows. Assess task clarity, hierarchy, state/feedback, recovery, accessibility, responsiveness, cost exposure and applicable implementation risks.

Use a compact cognitive walkthrough: What is the goal? Can the action be found and understood? Is its consequence clear? Is feedback intelligible? Can an error be recovered?

Select only relevant rules from `.prism-rebuild/knowledge/rules.json`; consult `.prism-rebuild/docs/ACCESSIBILITY-AND-PERFORMANCE.md` for applicable checks. Do not load all sources or invent universal psychology scores.

Reproduce a material defect where feasible and record exact steps, expected/actual behaviour, impact and evidence. Distinguish confirmed defect, inferred risk, preference and proposed enhancement. Verify time-sensitive technical claims with current primary documentation.

## Mode, outputs and exit

Guided and YOLO do not change the evidence standard. Return prioritized findings with affected versions, source/check evidence, confidence, remedy and acceptance condition. Identify strengths worth preserving and tradeoffs that require a design decision. Human participant research is deferred; do not manufacture observations or claim a screenshot proves interaction correctness.

Exit when the requested scope is assessed with explicit coverage and limitations. Missing tools or unavailable sources remain identified gaps. Assessment alone creates no approval or authority to implement.
